    "chunk_text": "10Bills of Exchange (Amendment) Act, No. 13 of 2025\n\n82D. The following shall be treated as conclusive evidence of a cheque dishonoured due to the insufficiency of funds in the account of the drawer: -\n\n(b) the deposit slip acknowledged by the collecting bank; or\n\n(c) the cheque returned by the drawee bank.\n\n82E. It shall be presumed unless the contrary is proved, that the payee or holder in due course of the cheque received the cheque for the discharge, in whole or in part, of any debt or other liability of the drawer.\n\n82F. Where a body of persons is convicted for an offence under this Ordinance, then \u2013\n\n(a) if that body of persons is a body corporate, every director, manager, or secretary of that body corporate at the time of the commission of such offence;\n\n(b) if that body of persons is a firm, every partner of that firm at the time of the commission of such offence; and\n\n(c) if that body of persons is an unincorporated body, every individual who is a member of such unincorporated body at the time of the commission of such offence,\n\nshall be deemed to have committed that offence:\n\nPresumption in favour of the payee or holder in due course of the cheque.\n\nOffences by a body of persons.\n\nConclusive evidence of a dishonoured cheque.\n\n11Bills of Exchange (Amendment) Act, No. 13 of 2025\n\nProvided however, any director, manager or secretary of such body corporate or any partner of such firm or any individual of such unincorporated body shall not be deemed to have committed such offence if he proves to the satisfaction of the court that such offence was committed without his knowledge or that he exercised all due diligence to prevent the commission of such offence.\u201d.\n\n17. Section 83 of the principal enactment is hereby amended by the repeal of all the words from \u201cFor the purpose of this section\u201d to the end of that section.\n\n18. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail."
